🎯 I found the primary bug.

Your form field names do not match what your controller expects.

Bug #1 (This is preventing the prediction from saving)
In your form you have:
<input
    class="form-control mb-3"
    type="text"
    name="predictionTip"
    placeholder="Prediction"
    required>
But your controller is expecting:

const {
    ...
    prediction: predictionTip,
    ...
} = req.body;
That means it is looking for:

req.body.prediction
NOT

req.body.predictionTip
So predictionTip becomes undefined.

Then this validation fails:

requiredFields.some(field => !field)
and the controller simply renders the form again.

✅ Fix Option 1 (Recommended)
Rename the input:

<input
    class="form-control mb-3"
    type="text"
    name="prediction"
    placeholder="Prediction"
    required>
Then your controller works without changes.

Bug #2
You commented out the Status dropdown.

Your controller still requires it.

You have:

status,
inside

requiredFields
But your form no longer sends a status.

So this is always undefined.

Either restore:

