which one is mongoose document variable?

Good question. It's this variable here:

const prediction = new Prediction({
    country,
    league,
    homeTeam,
    awayTeam,
    prediction: predictionTip,
    analysis,
    odds,
    confidence,
    isPremium: isPremium === "true",
    status,
    kickoffTime,
    cardNumber,
    result,
    createdBy: req.session.user._id
});
The variable named prediction is a Mongoose document. It's an instance of your Prediction model.

The problem is that you also have a field named prediction in your schema:

prediction: {
    type: String,
    required: true
}
So in the same function, you have:

const {
    prediction,
    ...
} = req.body;
and later:

const prediction = new Prediction(...);
Those two uses of the same name can easily cause confusion and led directly to the 
"Cannot access 'prediction' before initialization" error we debugged.

I recommend this naming convention
Instead of:

const prediction = new Prediction({
    ...
});
use:

const newPrediction = new Prediction({
    country,
    league,
    homeTeam,
    awayTeam,
    prediction,
    analysis,
    odds,
    confidence,
    isPremium: isPremium === "true",
    status,
    kickoffTime,
    cardNumber,
    result,
    createdBy: req.session.user._id
});

await newPrediction.save();
Or, if you prefer:

const predictionDoc = new Prediction({
    ...
});

await predictionDoc.save();
Both are common conventions.

Why this is better
Now each name has a single purpose:

Prediction → the Mongoose model (class).

prediction → the string from the form (e.g. "Ov 2.5").

newPrediction (or predictionDoc) → the document object that gets saved to MongoDB.

This makes the code much easier to read and prevents variable shadowing issues.

If I were reviewing the code for production, I'd write it like this:

const {
    country,
    league,
    homeTeam,
    awayTeam,
    prediction,
    analysis,
    odds,
    confidence,
    isPremium,
    kickoffTime,
    cardNumber,
    result
} = req.body;

const newPrediction = new Prediction({
    country,
    league,
    homeTeam,
    awayTeam,
    prediction,
    analysis,
    odds,
    confidence,
    isPremium: isPremium === "true",
    kickoffTime,
    cardNumber,
    result,
    createdBy: req.session.user._id
});

await newPrediction.save();
This version is cleaner, avoids the earlier bug entirely, 
and is the style I'd recommend as you continue building Prof Predict.


