The Edit and Update buttons serve different purposes and appear in different places.

1. Edit button (on the prediction cards) ✅
This button belongs on home.ejs, where the predictions are listed.

For each prediction card, you should have something like:

<% if (user && (user.role === "superuser" || user.role === "admin")) { %>

    <a href="/predictions/<%= prediction._id %>/edit"
       class="btn btn-warning btn-sm">
        Edit
    </a>

    <form action="/predictions/<%= prediction._id %>/delete"
          method="POST"
          style="display:inline;">
        <button class="btn btn-danger btn-sm">
            Delete
        </button>
    </form>

<% } %>
When you click Edit, it opens homeForm.ejs.

2. Update button (inside the form) ✅
You already have this:

<button class="btn btn-success w-100" type="submit">
    <%= prediction ? "Update Prediction" : "Add Prediction" %>
</button>
This button is dynamic:

When prediction is null (creating a new prediction), it displays:

Add Prediction
When prediction contains a prediction object (editing), it displays:

Update Prediction
So you do not need two separate buttons.

Why you're still seeing "Add Prediction"
At the moment, you're probably opening the form through:

/predictions/new
or

/auth/homeForm
In both cases, you're rendering:

prediction: null
so EJS displays:

Add Prediction
Only when you click:

/predictions/:id/edit
and your editPrediction() controller loads the prediction from MongoDB and passes it to the view:

res.render("homeForm", {
    pageTitle: "Edit Prediction",
    prediction
});
will the form:

pre-fill all the fields,

change the heading (if you make it dynamic),

