It is almost always one of these:

1. Function doesn't exist in the controller
Example:

router.get("/yesterday", authController.yesterdaysresults);
but your controller has

exports.yesterdayResults = ...
Notice:

yesterdaysresults
vs

yesterdayResults
One letter different = undefined.

2. Forgot exports
Example:

const yesterdaysresults = async (...) => {}
instead of

exports.yesterdaysresults = async (...) => {}
3. Misspelled import
Example:

const authController = require("../controller/authController");
instead of

const authController = require("../controllers/authController");
4. Syntax error above the function
If there is a missing brace } or missing ); before the function, Node never reaches

exports.yesterdaysresults = ...
making it undefined.

